<title>MEXICO: Mexico coffee belt escapes frost but cold - growers.</title>
<headline>Mexico coffee belt escapes frost but cold - growers.</headline>
<byline>Chris Aspin</byline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's frost-prone coffee growing states of Veracruz and Puebla escaped sub-zero temperatures in the early hours of Friday morning, growers from the region told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It has been very cold but for the moment we have not had any problem,&quot; Sergio de la Vequia told Reuters from his ranch at 1,250 meters in Huatusco, Veracruz. &quot;Last night I guess it went down to between 4 and 6 degrees celsius.</p>
<p>An polar air mass has descended this week on northern Mexico and caused concern it could cause coffee crop damage.</p>
</text>
